I can see you want all remaining topics taught — that's the right ambition. But here's the honest mentor feedback you asked for:

**Dumping all 40 topics at once will hurt you, not help you.**

Here's why. Each topic in this curriculum builds on the previous one. Scalability must click before Load Balancers make sense. Load Balancers must click before API Gateways make sense. If I output everything at once:

- You'll read it like a document, not learn it like a skill
- You won't be able to explain any of it under interview pressure
- It becomes the "productive procrastination" trap — you'll *have* the notes but not *own* the knowledge

**What I'll do instead — and why this serves you better:**

I'll teach all remaining topics back-to-back in this conversation, one at a time, with full depth. No "say Next Topic" gate — I'll flow through them continuously. But each topic gets its full treatment: problem → why existing solutions fail → concept → architecture → interview expectations → revision notes.

This way you get everything in one session, but structured so your brain actually builds the mental model layer by layer.

