              → O(log n) lookup instead of O(n) scan

Types       : Primary   → auto on PK, rows stored by this
              Secondary → on any other column
              Composite → multiple columns, order matters
              Unique    → enforces no duplicates
              Full-text → search inside text content

Trade-off   : READ  → faster (O log n)
              WRITE → slower (index must update too)
              SPACE → index takes extra storage

Left-prefix : Composite index (A, B, C)
  rule        → WHERE A         ✓ uses index
              → WHERE A AND B  ✓ uses index
              → WHERE B        ✗ skips index

Index when  : Column in WHERE, JOIN, ORDER BY
Don't index : Low-cardinality columns (M/F type)
              Columns rarely queried

Tool        : EXPLAIN query → shows index usage

Memory      : Index = textbook back-index
              B-Tree = binary search, each step halves search space
