              Primary → accepts writes
              Replicas → serve reads

Types       : Synchronous  → wait for replica ack
                             (no data loss, slower)
              Asynchronous → replicate in background
                             (fast, risk of data loss)
              Semi-sync    → wait for 1 replica ack

Solves      : Read scalability + High availability
Does NOT    : Solve write scalability (all writes → Primary)

Replication : Replica lags behind Primary
Lag           Can serve stale data
              Solution: route "read your own writes" to Primary

Failover    : Primary crashes → promote replica → reconfigure
              Automated by: AWS RDS Multi-AZ, MySQL Group Replication

