              WITHIN one database server

vs Sharding : Sharding = multiple servers
              Partitioning = one server, organized

Types       : Range → by value range (dates, IDs)
              Hash  → even distribution
              List  → by discrete values (country)

Pruning     : Query filter on partition key
              → DB scans only relevant partitions
              → massive speedup for range queries

Best for    : Time-series data, logs, events
              Large tables with date-range queries
              Easy archival (drop entire partition)

Memory      : Partitioning = labeled file drawers
              in ONE cabinet
              Sharding = multiple cabinets in
              different rooms
