Definition  : Producer → Queue → Consumer (async)
              Buffer between services

Benefits    : Decoupling (don't know each other)
              Async (producer doesn't wait)
              Durability (messages persist)
              Load leveling (absorbs spikes)

Patterns    : Point-to-Point → one consumer per message
              Pub/Sub (Topic) → all consumers get message

ACK         : Consumer signals success → queue deletes msg
              No ACK (crash) → message redelivered
              Guarantees: at-least-once delivery

Real example: Uber → ride request → matching, notification,
              analytics all decoupled via queue

Analogy     : Restaurant order tickets on a rail
              Waiter (producer) → rail (queue) → chef (consumer)
