              Always AFTER authentication

Models      : RBAC → roles → permissions (most common)
              ABAC → attributes of user+resource+env
              ACL  → per-resource access list (Google Drive)

RBAC        : User → Role(s) → Permission(s)
              Simple, widely understood

HTTP codes  : 401 = Not authenticated (who are you?)
              403 = Not authorized (you can't do that)

JWT authz   : Role/permissions in token
              No DB lookup → stateless authorization

Spring      : @PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')")
Security      Method-level authorization

Key rule    : Never enforce authorization without
              authentication first
